From b78125ced02e107ec42ed2bc2a6dba5101ba1d26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mateusz Bajorski <mbajorski@shasta.cloud>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 16:36:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mkimage-raw-efi: bump IMGB minimum to 2 GB for in-place
 upgrades

ROOTFS_PART_SIZE_MIN governs the size floor for both IMGA and IMGB.
IMGB also takes this floor verbatim because ROOTFS_IMG_B is empty
for non-evaluation kvm builds (see line 134), so the partition is
allocated as a placeholder for future upgrades.

At the old 512 MB floor, IMGB could not accept a copy of the active
rootfs (currently ~1.03 GB), forcing every OS upgrade through a USB
reinstall. Bump the floor to 2 GB so an inactive rootfs of up to 2 GB
fits without repartitioning, enabling the Fix F SSH dd-to-IMGB upgrade
flow. Cost on disk: ~3 GB shaved from the persist partition (475 GB ->
~473 GB).

Signed-off-by: Mateusz Bajorski <mbajorski@shasta.cloud>
---
 pkg/mkimage-raw-efi/make-raw | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pkg/mkimage-raw-efi/make-raw b/pkg/mkimage-raw-efi/make-raw
index 007ee9848..a39c701c7 100755
--- a/pkg/mkimage-raw-efi/make-raw
+++ b/pkg/mkimage-raw-efi/make-raw
@@ -99,7 +99,11 @@ EFI_PART_SIZE=$((36 * 1024 * 1024))
 # Warning: fixing the EVE upgrade logic, which should find
 # Warning: free space and rellocate all tables if image has
 # Warning: been bloated.
-ROOTFS_PART_SIZE_MIN=$((512 * 1024 * 1024))
+# OLG: bumped from 512 MB to 2 GB so IMGB is pre-sized for in-place
+# A/B rootfs upgrades over SSH (dd new rootfs to inactive part).
+# The current OLG rootfs is ~1.03 GB; 2 GB gives ~2x headroom and
+# costs ~3 GB out of the persist partition.
+ROOTFS_PART_SIZE_MIN=$((2 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024))
 # For eve-k lets set partition size to 4GB and EFI partition size to 2GB
 # Check if file /root/etc/eve-hv-type exists.
 # make-raw will be called twice during compilation and during installation.
